    {
      "title": "US officials recover audio from ‘Mississippi miracle’ cruise ship and tanker crash",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/audio-new-orleans-mississippi-river-cruise-tanker-crash",
      "description": "<p>Tank vessel suffered sudden steering failure two minutes before slamming into docked riverboat near New Orleans</p><p>Federal safety investigators with the National Transportation Safety Board (NTSB) recovered audio and released a preliminary timeline on Sunday of a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/13/mississippi-river-crash-new-orleans\">collision</a> between a cruise ship and a tanker vessel in the Mississippi River on Friday.</p><p>The data was retrieved after more than 30 people were injured when a tanker collided with a docked cruise ship – American Cruise Lines’ <a href=\"https://www.americancruiselines.com/ships/paddlewheeler-cruise-ships/american-heritage\">American Heritage riverboat</a> – near the port of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-orleans\">New Orleans</a> on Friday at about 12.30pm. All passengers aboard the cruise ship have been accounted for, officials said.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/15/audio-new-orleans-mississippi-river-cruise-tanker-crash\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
